OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FSpecialist glasses have sold out at
OL,8,Fmajor retailers as Britons prepare for
OL,9,Fthe best solar eclipse in decades.
OL,11,FMore than 90% of the sun will be
OL,12,Fobscured by the moon between 6.17pm
OL,13,Fand 8.06pm on Wednesday, the most it
OL,14,Fhas been blocked above UK skies since
OL,15,Fthe total eclipse in 1999.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30402
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FConvenience stores, national parks and
OL,8,Fthe Royal Greenwich Observatory have
OL,9,Fall exhausted their glasses supplies
OL,10,Fahead of the eclipse, which will be
OL,11,Fthe country's fullest for the next 54
OL,12,Fyears.
OL,14,FThe Royal Greenwich Observatory told
OL,15,Fthe Press Association it had sold
OL,16,Fapproximately 15,000 pairs of eclipse
OL,17,Fglasses ` a sellout ` in the last
OL,18,Fmonth.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G2/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30403
SC,0003
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FMeanwhile, consumers have been warned
OL,8,Fagainst using "knock-off" glasses to
OL,9,Fwatch the event and eye doctors urged
OL,10,Fpeople to avoid looking directly at
OL,11,Fthe sun, with even brief exposure
OL,12,Fcausing lasting vision damage.
OL,14,FOnly special solar eclipse glasses
OL,15,Fthat are ISO 12312-2 certified for the
OL,16,Fsafest eye protection should be used
OL,17,Fto view the eclipse and sunglasses are
OL,18,Fnot sufficient, experts said.
OL,26,@pD@OOUpD@YO]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30404
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FFollowing the 1999 total solar
OL,8,Feclipse, the Royal College of
OL,9,FOphthalmologists reported around 70
OL,10,Fcases of people experiencing vision
OL,11,Fproblems after watching the eclipse.
OL,13,FAround 40% had looked at it for less
OL,14,Fthan a minute.
OL,16,FMohamed Elalfy, a consultant
OL,17,Fophthalmologist and president of the
OL,18,FRoyal College of Ophthalmologists,
OL,19,Fsaid: "The safest way to enjoy the
OL,20,Feclipse is to observe it indirectly,
OL,21,Fsuch as by watching a live broadcast.
OL,26,@{D@GOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30405
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,F"Looking directly at the sun during a
OL,8,Fsolar eclipse can cause damage to the
OL,9,Fretina, potentially damaging the cells
OL,10,Fresponsible for sharp central vision.
OL,12,F"Crucially, the retina has no pain
OL,13,Freceptors, so people will not feel the
OL,14,Fdamage as it happens.
OL,16,F"Symptoms may only become apparent
OL,17,Fseveral hours later and can include
OL,18,Fblurred vision, a central blind or
OL,19,Fdark spot, distorted vision, reduced
OL,20,Fcolour perception and increased
OL,21,Fsensitivity to light.
OL,26,@oD@AOUtD@AOUxD@AOU
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G5/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30406
SC,0006
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,F"While some people recover over weeks
OL,8,For months, others can be left with
OL,9,Fpermanent visual impairment."
OL,11,FDevon, Cornwall and the westernmost
OL,12,Fparts of Pembrokeshire in Wales are
OL,13,Fset to see the eclipse at its fullest,
OL,14,Fwith a range of 94% to 96% of the sun
OL,15,Fobscured by the moon.
OL,17,FPlymouth in particular is forecast to
OL,18,Fsee the moon cover 94.66% of the sun
OL,19,Fat 7.16pm on Wednesday, according to
OL,20,Fthe Met Office.
OL,26,@oD@AOUqD@]O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G6/10
