PN,30407
SC,0007
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FThe rest of Wales, Northern Ireland,
OL,8,Fparts of the West Midlands and the
OL,9,FSouth West, and the westernmost parts
OL,10,Fof Scotland can expect to see 92% to
OL,11,F94% solar coverage.
OL,13,FIn Cardiff, the moon is forecast to
OL,14,Fobscure 93.24% of the sun at 7.13pm
OL,15,Fwhile in Belfast it will cover 93.09%
OL,16,Fof the sun at 7.08pm.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G7/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,305,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30408
SC,0008
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F304A1786497480
OL,3,CSpecialist glasses sell out as Britons
OL,4,Cprepare for best solar eclipse in
OL,5,Cdecades
OL,7,FSkygazers in the rest of the UK will
OL,8,Flikely see the moon obscure 90% to 92%
OL,9,Fof the sun ` with 91.79% expected in
OL,10,FBirmingham at 7.12pm, 91.41% in London
OL,11,Fat 7.13pm, 90.74% in Inverness at
OL,12,F7.03pm, 90.71% in Edinburgh at 7.06pm
OL,13,Fand 90.22% in Newcastle at 7.07pm.
OL,15,FThose most keen to catch a sight of
OL,16,Fthe fullest possible solar eclipse
OL,17,Fshould avoid the easternmost parts of
OL,18,Fthe UK, where only 88% to 90% of solar
OL,19,Fcoverage is expected.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G8/10
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
